winemac: Implement cross-process MetalViewSwapChain via CALayerHost.

Upstream Wine commit 1a63b0d7c431f1ebbaba9afd2daa312690eb8020 by Marc-Aurel Zent
<mzent@codeweavers.com>, 2026-05-20, committed by Alexandre Julliard for wine-11.11.
It gives a process a Metal swapchain for a top-level window another process owns: the
renderer draws into an offscreen CAMetalLayer exported through a CAContext, and the
owner hosts it in its NSWindow with a CALayerHost when asked to by
WM_MACDRV_CREATE_REMOTE_LAYER. That is the half of Steam's problem upstream has already
solved; the child-window half is the next patch. Drop this one together with 0003 when
the base catches up.

One hunk placed by hand: the _caLayerHosts ivar of WineContentView, because CrossOver's
version of that block carries the CW HACK 22435 ivar after _metalView and the upstream
context does not match.

